  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nA weak cut-off low looks to remain centered over the region through \nSaturday. This feature will keep temperatures slightly below \nseasonal normals, along with periodic chances (15-30 percent) for \nrain showers and isolated afternoon thunderstorms, primarily over \nthe higher terrain of eastern Oregon and southwest Idaho. While \nwidespread heavy precipitation is not expected due to limited \nmoisture transport initially, moisture does look to increase later \nin the week as more monsoonal moisture is pulled into the low. Thus, \ngreater potential for heavier rainfall exists, especially across the \ncentral Idaho mountains. By Sunday, ensemble clusters show \nincreasing divergence regarding the evolution of the pattern. A \nsubset of cluster guidance maintains a secondary longwave trough \ndropping out of the Gulf of Alaska, which would prolong cool \ntemperatures and unsettled shower activity. Conversely, other \ndeterministic solutions favor the advancement of a flat high-\npressure ridge from the Great Basin, leading to a warmer and drier \npattern heading into early next week. Given the high uncertainty \ninherent to cut-off systems, forecast confidence remains low for the \nSunday period.",
